module gunbc.floor_arm_set_consumer_seed_growth

import gunbc.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// FORWARD-FREEZE RECEIPT for the hand Rust that makes the required floor honest on the
// stale-match class (gunbc#11194; gunbc#11256, restoring gunbc#11252's invocation half and adding
// the dependents half on top of it). gunbc.seed_growth_admission
// seed_growth_forward_freeze_policy_note makes unenumerated hand growth in src/v1 a stop-line,
// so every added declaration is enumerated below; modified items keep their names and are not
// netted (ExistingSeedItemModified: ModuleDeclarationRecord, collect_reference_occurrences and
// record_from_module in declaration_index.rs; run_required_wave_admission; run_required_floor
// and changed_and_enrolled_witness_identities_with_index; assemble_prepared_subject_closure and
// prepare_repository_closure; the two run_required_floor call sites in bin/claim_executor.rs).
//
// WHY IT IS ADMITTED AGAINST THE v1 FREEZE, BY PURPOSE. gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing
// v1_seed_standing admits a change when it serves the v2 self-host program, and the required floor
// is the INSTRUMENT that guards that program. Today `check_match` refuses a non-exhaustive match
// under `gunbc compile` and on NO required lane: the floor prepares the gate closure plus what the
// diff names, so a match that goes stale because its coproduct grew an arm in another module has
// an empty diff at the match site and is never Strict-prepared. gunbc#11194 was caught by a person
// reading arms. This change makes a real wall reachable on the required path for that class, in
// both of its directions, through the ONE preparation the floor already runs -- no second
// checker, no second Strict path, no builtin, no admission row, no public export.
//
// WHY IT IS RUST AND NOT .dag. The consumption relation is `declaring_candidates` over
// `ModuleDeclarationRecord`, a host-only carrier (gunbc.declaration_index_seed_growth CLASS A:
// the input type is host Rust and there is no .dag per-module record yet). The selector is a pure
// fold over two of those indexes and FOLLOWS that carrier's migration rather than forking it. The
// base side is reconstructed from git blobs, which is the scm lane's acquisition boundary (CLASS
// B). The DECISIONS the selector makes are modeled in v2.workflow.floor_subject_seed
// (`arm_set_match_read_disposition`, `arm_set_match_consumer_binding`, the seed grounds and the
// typed out-of-root dispositions), and the host is their wire rendering.
//
// gunbc#11408 (the probe-exclusion repair of the touched-entry seed) adds two more items under the
// same purpose: prepared_subject_exclusion_row_for, THE ONE exclusion predicate every consumer of a
// prepared-subject exclusion list now reads (closure assembly, whole-tree strict resolve, the
// floor inventory walk, the planning receipt) in place of four same-shaped copies, and the RED
// that an edited must-not-resolve probe is seeded, reported against its row, and not prepared.
// module_seeds_from_touched_entry_files and floor_prepared_subject_exclusions are
// ExistingSeedItemModified there (the helper returns its seeded pairs; the roster gains one row).
//
// HAND-ITEM DELTA is derived from the diff by gunbc.rust_item_host_observation and is not
// restated here. The test items are enumerated because they are hand declarations in the seed;
// the executed red among them is arm_growth_selects_the_untouched_match_consumer_and_strict_
// preparation_refuses_it, the #11194 shape end to end, with its positive control beside it.
data floor_arm_set_consumer_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.namespace_baseline", decl_name: "BaselineReconstruction", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.namespace_baseline", decl_name: "reconstruct_base_index", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.namespace_baseline", decl_name: "ArmSetChange", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.namespace_baseline", decl_name: "ArmConsumerBinding", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.namespace_baseline", decl_name: "ArmSetMatchConsumer", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.namespace_baseline", decl_name: "ArmSetConsumerSelection", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.namespace_baseline", decl_name: "arm_set_changed_match_consumers", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "module_name_is_or_is_contained_by", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "prepared_subject_exclusion_row_for", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "FloorDiffProjections", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "CompileSubjectSeeds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "ArmSetConsumerPlanning", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "arm_set_consumer_planning", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "module_seeds_from_touched_entry_files", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "floor_source_roots_workspace_relative", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner", decl_name: "path_under_floor_roots", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "helper_fn_file_seeds_its_authored_module", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "helper_fn_file_outside_floor_roots_is_a_typed_disposition_not_a_seed", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "helper_fn_file_without_module_header_refuses_rather_than_skipping", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "ARM_X_BASE", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "ARM_X_HEAD", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "ARM_Y", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "ARM_W", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "ARM_Z", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "REC_BASE", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "REC_HEAD", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "REC_USER", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "WORKSPACE_CWD", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "enter_workspace_cwd", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "leave_workspace_cwd", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "arm_set_fixture", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "arm_set_index", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "arm_set_selection", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "consumers_of", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "arm_growth_selects_the_untouched_match_consumer_and_strict_preparation_refuses_it", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "arm_growth_consumer_with_a_wildcard_is_planned_and_prepares_clean", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "a_type_change_with_no_match_consumers_plans_nothing_extra", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "a_diff_with_no_arm_set_change_plans_nothing_extra", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "arm_removal_selects_the_consumer_that_still_names_the_arm", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "a_module_seed_is_segment_bounded", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner.changed_witness_projection_tests", decl_name: "an_edited_must_not_resolve_probe_is_seeded_then_excluded_and_preparation_stays_green", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],
  reason: "A required floor that never Strict-prepares an untouched module cannot run check_match on it, so a coproduct growing an arm elsewhere makes an exhaustive match silently stale (gunbc#11194). Two halves: seed the touched module (dependency direction, gunbc#11252) and seed the match-bearing consumers of a coproduct whose arm set changed between the floor's own resolved diff base and head (dependents direction), derived from the consumption relation declaring_candidates over the parse phase's DeclarationIndex, lifted by two record fields (per-coproduct arm sets, match-arm constructor occurrences) and never a second relation -- and prepared through the SAME closure path. reconstruct_base_index is the base-side reconstruction the deleted wave-admission wall shared, lifted so both callers shared it; the wall is gone (operator ruling 2026-09-19, gunbc.rung_drop namespace_wave_admission_wall_removed) and the floor's planning row is the remaining caller, with the items now homed in v1_compiler.namespace_baseline and parameterized on the window because the floor compares against v2.workflow.floor_diff_observe's baseline. module_name_is_or_is_contained_by is the segment-bounded rule for module-name seeds (a.b seeds a.b and a.b.c, never a.bc); gate PREFIXES stay textual as site disposition reads them. Out-of-root touched files and consumers are typed rows, not counts.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "The selector, its records and the planning enum follow gunbc.declaration_index_seed_growth's first step: the moment the per-module declaration record is a .dag carrier, arm_set_changed_match_consumers is an ordinary fold over it beside declaring_candidates and moves with them, and v2.workflow.floor_subject_seed consumes it directly instead of being mirrored. reconstruct_base_index follows the scm lane with git_stdout and base_records: when a typed repository-read transport can supply a file's text at a ref. The seed-list plumbing in run_required_floor and module_name_is_or_is_contained_by dissolve when preparation is a modeled operation over PreparedSubjectSeedGround rather than two string lists. The tests are the evidence and retire only as regression controls when the wall climbs; a fixture that greens when the invocation lands flips to a permanent control, it does not retire.",
  current_boundary: "Reachable only from the required floor's planning row (run_required_floor, witnesses lane); the wall's own runner is deleted with the wall (operator ruling 2026-09-19). Decides nothing for gunbc compile, claim_batch or any per-entry path. Widens the prepared subject by exactly the touched modules and the match-bearing consumers of changed coproducts, each announced with its ground on the run's own receipt line, and narrows nothing: a base that cannot be reconstructed on a CI commit REFUSES the floor rather than planning blind, and a local run without a diff baseline reports the projection unevaluated exactly as the changed-witness projection already does."
}
